From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geert Geurts <geert@verweggistan.eu>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Run scriptlets with the PATH rpm was started with

rpm replaces PATH with a fixed /sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/X11R6/bin
before it runs scriptlets and helpers such as sysusers.sh, unless
%_install_script_path is defined.

The tuxifier installer runs rpm from a conda environment (python-nest) in an
initramfs, with --root pointing at the new system. sysusers.sh needs touch,
basename and xargs. They are in the environment's bin directory, which the
caller puts on PATH, but not in the initramfs's /usr/bin, nor in the target
root before coreutils and findutils are installed. With the fixed PATH they
fail with "command not found".

Use the PATH from the environment when it is set. An explicit
%_install_script_path still takes precedence.
---
 lib/rpmscript.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/rpmscript.cc b/lib/rpmscript.cc
--- a/lib/rpmscript.cc
+++ b/lib/rpmscript.cc
@@ -273,6 +273,20 @@
 
     {   char *ipath = rpmExpand("%{_install_script_path}", NULL);
 	const char *path = SCRIPT_PATH;
+	const char *envpath = getenv("PATH");
+
+	/*
+	 * Prefer the PATH rpm itself was started with over the built-in
+	 * default. When rpm runs from a conda environment (python-nest in the
+	 * tuxifier initramfs) with --root, the helpers it runs, such as
+	 * sysusers.sh, need touch, basename and xargs. Those live in the
+	 * environment's bin directory and exist in neither the initramfs's
+	 * /usr/bin nor, early in the transaction, in the target root, so with
+	 * the fixed default PATH they are "command not found". An explicit
+	 * %_install_script_path below still takes precedence.
+	 */
+	if (envpath && *envpath)
+	    path = envpath;
 
 	if (ipath && ipath[5] != '%')
 	    path = ipath;
